Short answer ‚Äî the code path that sends the ‚Äúmonitor is down‚Äù (and escalation) emails:

- Scheduler / trigger for escalation emails
  - `server/src/service/infrastructure/notificationsService.ts`
    - Function: `scheduleEscalationNotifications(...)` (schedules escalation sends)
    - Function: `handleNotifications(...)` (called when a monitor goes down ‚Äî it sends immediate alerts and calls the scheduler)

- Message builder (creates the email content/subject/body)
  - `server/src/service/infrastructure/notificationMessageBuilder.ts`
    - Function: `buildMessage(...)` ‚Äî determines `type`, `severity` and `content` used by providers

- Email provider (formats and sends provider-specific message)
  - `server/src/service/infrastructure/notificationProviders/email.ts`
    - Function: `sendMessage(notification, message)` ‚Äî builds subject and HTML and calls email service
    - `buildSubject(...)` ‚Äî where the subject is composed (we added the `Escalation:` prefix when `message.metadata.escalation` is set)
    - `buildEmailFromMessage(...)` ‚Äî builds HTML using templates

- Low-level SMTP send
  - `server/src/service/infrastructure/emailService.ts`
    - Function: `sendEmail(to, subject, html)` ‚Äî actually sends via nodemailer (SMTP)

If you want to:
- Inspect logs when an escalation fires, watch the server console around `NotificationsService` and `EmailProvider` logs.
- Change text (subject/body) update `EmailProvider.buildSubject` or `notificationMessageBuilder.buildContent`.
- Replace the in-memory scheduler with durable queue work, modify `SuperSimpleQueueHelper` / enqueue jobs instead of `setTimeout` in `notificationsService`.

