What I changed and why
- Previously the code invoked incident handling without awaiting its result, so there was no reliable place to inspect the created incident and schedule escalation sends. I now await the result from `incidentService.handleIncident(...)`.
- If an incident was created and the monitor has an `escalation` config (with `channelId` and `delayMinutes`), the helper schedules a one-time in-memory timer to run after the configured delay (delayMinutes). When the timer fires it re-checks that the incident is still active and then calls `notificationsService.sendEscalationNotification(...)`.
- Added logging for scheduling, execution, skips, and failures so you can trace escalation behavior in the logs.

Notes and recommendations
- This uses an in-memory timer. If the server process restarts before the timer fires, the escalation will not run. For production reliability you should enqueue escalation jobs in a durable queue (Redis, DB, or existing Scheduler) instead of setTimeout ‚Äî I can help add that.
- Confirm your monitor documents include the `escalation` object (persisted shape) with `delayMinutes` and `channelId`. If your frontend stores escalation using a different key/shape, ensure you map it into `monitor.escalation` when saving.
- After applying this patch restart the server and reproduce: create/edit a monitor to set escalation.delayMinutes = 1 and escalation.channelId to the notification id, then force a down check or call the test endpoint. Watch logs for the "Scheduling escalation send" and later "Executing escalation send" entries.®Mentionsê®MetadataÅªvscopilot_reserved_chatModeì≠System.Stringƒ£Ask¬¨EventMessage¿©SessionIdíŸ$c7b05e86-4c00-44d7-b228-bd27acc92949Å¢IdŸ4Microsoft.VisualStudio.Conversations.Chat.HelpWindow¶AuthorÉ§NameÆGitHub Copilot§IconÇ§GuidŸ$ae27a6b0-e345-4288-96df-5eaf394ee369¢IdÕÕßServiceÇ§NameŸ7Microsoft.VisualStudio.Copilot.CopilotChatAgentProviderßVersion£0.3¶Status•Modelí ﬁ ¢Id™gpt-5-mini§Name™gpt-5-mini´DisplayName™GPT-5 mini¶Family™gpt-5-mini¨Capabilities ´BillingType®Endpoint≥AdditionalEndpointsí•State•TermsŸêEnable access to the latest GPT-5 mini model from OpenAI. [Learn more about how GitHub Copilot serves GPT-5 mini](https://gh.io/copilot-openai).¨RestrictedToê™MultiplierÀ?      ÆUserSelectable√¨InfoMessagesêØWarningMessagesêØPurposesDefaultë∞PurposesFallbackê´InputTokensŒ Ûú®Encoding™o200k_base¶QuotasìÜ§Type©Timestamp◊ˇm◊Ÿ@i◊Œ©ResetTime÷ˇi˛y •UsageÀ@kÄ     •LimitÀ@@     ÆOverageAllowed¬Ü§Type©Timestamp◊ˇm◊Ÿ@i◊Œ©ResetTime÷ˇi˛y •UsageÀ        •LimitÀ@Ø@     ÆOverageAllowed¬Ü§Type©Timestamp◊ˇm◊Ÿ@i◊Œ©ResetTime÷ˇi˛y •UsageÀ        •LimitÀ        ÆOverageAllowed¬©FollowUpsëÇßMessageŸrWhat changes do I need to make to ensure the escalation notifications are reliably sent after the specified delay?ØSendImmediately¬®CanRetry√í ã≠CorrelationIdŸ$07d99eb4-b074-4721-87cf-2a9ed24e7116©MessageIdŸ$59144957-29ce-40e8-a632-3f469f407796ßContextêßContentëíÖ¢Idƒë∂âdeÙNø∑35™Õ$Á™Visibility´AnnotationsêßContentŸ%is this a bew file? it does not exist®Mentionsê®MetadataÅªvscopilot_reserved_chatModeì≠System.Stringƒ£Ask¬¨EventMessage¿¶Intent¿®Guidance¿•ModelÖ¶Family™gpt-5-minißModelId™gpt-5-mini¨Capabilities ®EndpointßPurpose≤DirectedRespondersëÇ§NameŸ7Micro