What I changed
- Added `escalationRules` to the base defaults returned by `useMonitorForm`.
- The hook now supports multiple persisted shapes:
  - Preferred: `data.escalationRules` (array of { notificationId, delayMinutes }).
  - Backwards/alternate: `escalationDelayMinutes` + `escalationNotificationId`, or `escalation: { delayMinutes, channelId }`.
- If an escalation channel is present it maps into the form as a single-element `escalationRules` array so the `EscalationRulesEditor` (which expects an array) will display the saved values.

How this fixes your issue
- Previously the form defaults did not include escalation values, so when editing a monitor the escalation inputs were reset/empty even though the monitor had escalation data saved. With this change the editor will show existing escalation values without needing to re-add them.

